## What's happening and why

**System prompt as the policy home**
The `SYSTEM_PROMPT` string is the only place that encodes the "always check before refunding" rule. A product manager can edit it without touching any code.

**The loop in one sentence**
Call the API → if the model wants tools, run them all and feed results back → repeat until `stop_reason == "end_turn"`.

```
user msg
   │
   ▼
 Claude ──stop_reason=tool_use──► run tools ──► append tool_results
   │                                                    │
   └──────────────────stop_reason=end_turn◄─────────────┘
         return text to customer
```

**Key details worth knowing**

| Thing | Why it matters |
|---|---|
| `messages.append` for *both* assistant and tool results | The API requires the full conversation history each call — don't drop either side |
| Loop over all blocks for `tool_use` | Claude can request multiple tools in one turn; handle them all before looping |
| `hasattr(block, "text")` not `block.type == "text"` | Defensive — works even if the SDK adds new block types |
| No retry / error handling | You said lean; add `tenacity` or a try/except around the API call when you're ready |

